mfd: retu-user: a charge failsafe under BME

Maemo BME charges through /dev/tahvo; if it dies or hangs mid-charge the
charge PWM stays where it was. The file that last set a non-zero PWM owns
the charge; the charger goes off (PWM 0, CHGCTL override to 0 %) when it
closes the device, when its process uses neither /dev/retu nor /dev/tahvo
for 12 s, after 6 h of PWM-on time in one charge (latched), or when Retu
reads the battery past ~4.45 V or its NTC past ~55 or below ~-5 degrees C
twice running (latched, and the device powered off). Catastrophe limits
only, with BME default calibration; BME and n810-guard keep the finer
ones.

The time cap counts PWM-on time, not time since the charge began: BME's
pulsed charging sets the PWM to 0 every minute or two to read the battery
at rest, and each would otherwise start the clock again. A charge ends
after 30 minutes with the PWM off.

--- a/drivers/mfd/retu-user.c
+++ b/drivers/mfd/retu-user.c
